{"total":157,"totalPage":4,"page":3,"pageSize":50,"items":[{"id":"69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b5ae","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":908,"bookHadithIndex":101,"text":"Aishah narrated:\"I twisted the garlands for the Hadi of the Prophet, then he did not assume Ihram, nor did he avoid any clothing","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-908-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-908-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-908-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-908-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c702dd1a4c9c86f0b5af","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":909,"bookHadithIndex":102,"text":"Aishah narrated:\"I twisted the garlands for all of the Hadi of the Messenger of Allah, which were sheep, then he did not assume Ihram","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-909-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-909-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5b0","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":910,"bookHadithIndex":103,"text":"Najiyah Al-Khuza'i (the Companion of the Messenger of Allah) said:\"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What should be done with the afflicted among the Hadi?' He said: 'Slaughter them, then dip their sandals in their blood, then leave them so that the people can eat them","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-910-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-910-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-910-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-910-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5b1","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":911,"bookHadithIndex":104,"text":"Anas bin Malik narrated:That the Prophet saw a man driving his Badanah so he said to him: \"Ride it.\" He said: \"O Messenger of Allah! It is a Badanah.\" So on the third or fourth time he said to him: \"Ride it. And woe to you","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-911-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-911-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-911-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-911-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5b2","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":912,"bookHadithIndex":105,"text":"Anas bin Malik narrted:\"When the Messenger of Allah stoned the Jamrah, he slaughtered his sacrifice, then he presented the barber the right side (of his head) and he shaved it, then he gave (the hair) to Abu Talhah. Then he presented the left side to him and he shaved it. Then he said: 'Divide it (the hair) among the people","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-912-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-912-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-912-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5b3","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":913,"bookHadithIndex":106,"text":"Ibn Umar narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \"May Allah have mercy upon those who shaved\" saying it one or two times, then he said: \"And those who shortened","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-913-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-913-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-913-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-913-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5b4","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":914,"bookHadithIndex":107,"text":"Ali narrated:\"The Messenger of Allah prohibited that a woman should shave her head","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-914-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-914-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-914-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Hasan"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5b5","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":915,"bookHadithIndex":108,"text":"(Another chain) with similar (as no. 914) from Khilas:But he did not mention \"from Ali","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-915-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Hasan"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5b6","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":916,"bookHadithIndex":109,"text":"Abdullah bin Amr narrated:\"A man asked the Messenger of Allah: 'I shaved before slaughtering.' So he said: 'Slaughter, and there is no harm.' Another man asked him: 'I performed the sacrifice before stoning.' He said: 'Stone, and there is no harm","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-916-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-916-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-916-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-916-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5b7","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":917,"bookHadithIndex":110,"text":"Aishah narrated:\"I put perfume with musk in it on the Messenger of Allah before he assumed Ihram, and on the Day of An-Nahr before he performed Tawaf around the House","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-917-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-917-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-917-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-917-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5b8","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":918,"bookHadithIndex":111,"text":"Al-Fadl bin Abbas narrated:\"I was a companion rider with the Messenger of Allah from Jam to Mina. He did not cease saying the Talbiyah until stoning Jamrat Al-Aqabah","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-918-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-918-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-918-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-918-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5b9","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":919,"bookHadithIndex":112,"text":"Ibn Abbas narrated:(that the Prophet): \"Would stop saying the Talbiyah during \"Umrah when he touched the (Black) Stone","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-919-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih Muquf"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-919-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih Muquf"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-919-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-919-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5ba","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":920,"bookHadithIndex":113,"text":"Aishah narrated:\"The Prophet delayed the visiting Tawaf until the night","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-920-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Shadh"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-920-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-920-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5bb","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":921,"bookHadithIndex":114,"text":"Ibn Umar narrated:\"The Prophet, Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman would camp at Al-Abtah","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-921-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-921-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-921-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-921-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5bc","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":922,"bookHadithIndex":115,"text":"Ibn Abbas narrated:\"At-Tahsib is nothing, it is only a place that the Messenger of Allah camped at","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-922-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-922-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-922-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-922-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5bd","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":923,"bookHadithIndex":116,"text":"Aishah narrated:\"The Messenger of Allah only camped at Al-Abtah because it was easier for his departure","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-923-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-923-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-923-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-923-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5be","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":924,"bookHadithIndex":117,"text":"Jabir bin Abdullah narrated:\"A woman held a boy of hers up for the Messenger of Allah and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Is there Hajj for this one' He said: 'Yes, and you will be rewarded","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-924-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-924-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-924-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5bf","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":925,"bookHadithIndex":118,"text":"As-Sa'ib bin Yazid narrated:\"My father took me for Hajj with the Messenger of Allah during the Farewell Hajj, and I was seven years old","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-925-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-925-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5c0","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":926,"bookHadithIndex":119,"text":"(Another chain) from Jabir bin Abdullah:From the Prophet, with similar (Hadith of Muhammad bin Tarif no)","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-926-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-926-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5c1","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":927,"bookHadithIndex":120,"text":"Jabir narrated:\"When we performed our Hajj with the Prophet we would say the Talbiyah for the women and we would stone for the boys","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-927-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-927-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-927-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5c2","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":928,"bookHadithIndex":121,"text":"Al-Fadl bin Abbas narrated:\"A woman from Khath'am said: 'O Messenger of Allah! My father has lived until Allah has made Hajj obligatory, and he is an elderly man who is not able to sit on the back of a camel.' So he (pbuh) said: 'Perform Hajj for him","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-928-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-928-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-928-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-928-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5c3","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":929,"bookHadithIndex":122,"text":"Abdullah bin Buraidah narrated from his father who said:\"A woman came to the Prophet and said: 'My mother died and she did not perform Hajj should I perform Hajj on her behalf?' He said: 'Yes, perform Hajj on her behalf","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-929-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-929-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-929-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-929-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Muslim"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5c4","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":930,"bookHadithIndex":123,"text":"Abu Razin Al-Uqaili narrated:That he went to the Prophet and said: \"O Messenger of Allah! My father is an elderly man who is not able to perform Hajj nor Umrah nor undertake a journey.' He said: 'Perform Hajj on behalf of your father and perform Umrah","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-930-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-930-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-930-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-930-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5c5","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":931,"bookHadithIndex":124,"text":"Jabir narrated that:The Prophet was asked about whether Umrah was obligatory? He said: \"No. But if you perform Umrah it is more virtuous","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-931-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Daif Isnaad"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-931-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif Isnaad"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-931-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5c6","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":932,"bookHadithIndex":125,"text":"Ibn Abbas narrated:That the Prophet said: \"Umrah has been entered into Hajj until the Day of Resurrection","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-932-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-932-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-932-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5c7","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":933,"bookHadithIndex":126,"text":"Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah said:\"Umrah to 'Umrah atones for the sins between them, and for A1-Hajj Al-Mabrur there is no reward except Paradise","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-933-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-933-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-933-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-933-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5c8","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":934,"bookHadithIndex":127,"text":"Amr bin Aws narrated from Abdur-Rahman bin Abi Bakr:\"The Prophet ordered Abdur-RAhman bin Abi Bakr to (accompany) Aishah to perform Umrah from At-Tan'im","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-934-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-934-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-934-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-934-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5c9","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":935,"bookHadithIndex":128,"text":"Muharrish Al-Kabi narrated:\"The Messenger of Allah left Al-Ji'irranah during the night for Umrah, then he entered Makkah during he night and performed his Umrah. Then he left there during the night, then he was in Al-Ji'irranah by the morning, as if he had spent the night. When the sun passed the zenith in the morning he left from the midst of Sarif until he came on a road from amidst Sarif. It is because of this that his Umrah was concealed from the people","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-935-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-935-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-935-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5ca","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":936,"bookHadithIndex":129,"text":"Urwah said:Ibn Umar was asked: In which month did the Messenger of Allah perform Umrah? He said: 'During Rajab.' So Aishah said: 'The Messenger of Allah did not perform Umrah except that he was with him - meaning Ibn Umar - and he did not ever perform Umrah in the month of Rajab","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-936-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-936-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-936-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5cb","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":937,"bookHadithIndex":130,"text":"Ibn Umar narrated:\"The Prophet performed Umrah four times, one of them was during Rajab","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-937-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-937-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-937-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-937-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Bukhari"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5cc","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":938,"bookHadithIndex":131,"text":"Al-Bara narrated:\"The Prophet performed Umrah during Dhul-Qa'dah","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-938-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-938-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-938-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-938-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5cd","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":939,"bookHadithIndex":132,"text":"Umm Ma'qil narrated that:The Prophet said: \"Umrah during Ramadan is equal to Hajj","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-939-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-939-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-939-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5ce","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":940,"bookHadithIndex":133,"text":"Ikrimah narrated from Al-Hajjaj bin Amr who narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \"Whoever suffers a fracture or becomes lame them he (leaves the state of Ihram) and is required to perform another Hajj.\" I (Ikrimah) mentioned that to Abu Hurairah and Ibn Abbas and they said: \"He told the truth","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-940-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-940-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-940-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5cf","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":941,"bookHadithIndex":134,"text":"Ibn Abbas narrated:\"Duba'ah bint Az-Zubair came to the prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I want to perform Hajj so should I state a condition?' He said: 'Yes.' She asked: 'So how should I say it?' He said: 'Say; \"Labbaik Allahumma labbaika mahilli minal Ard haithu tahbisuni (I respond to Your call O Allah, I respond to Your call, I will exit Ihram any where on the earth where You prevent me)","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-941-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-941-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-941-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-941-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Hasan"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5d0","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":942,"bookHadithIndex":135,"text":"Salim narrated that :His father disliked making a condition during Hajj and he said: 'Is not the Sunnah of your Prophet enough for you?","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-942-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-942-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-942-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-942-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Bukhari"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5d1","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":943,"bookHadithIndex":136,"text":"Aishah narrated:\"It was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah that Safiyyah bint Huyai got her menses during the days of Mina, so he said: \"Will she prevent us (from departing)?\" They said: \"She has done (Tawaf) Al-Ifadah/\" So the Messenger of Allah said: \"In that case there is no harm","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-943-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-943-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-943-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-943-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5d2","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":944,"bookHadithIndex":137,"text":"Ibn Umar said:\"Whoever performs Hajj to the House, then let the last of their acts be at the House, except for menstruating women. The Messenger of Allah gave them permission (to leave).\" (Sahih Mawquf)","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-944-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-944-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-944-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-944-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5d3","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":945,"bookHadithIndex":138,"text":"","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-945-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-945-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5d4","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":946,"bookHadithIndex":140,"text":"Al-Harith bin Abdullah bin Aws said:\"I heard the Prophet saying: 'Whoever performs Hajj to this House, or Umrah, then let the last of his acts be at the House'\" So Umar said: \"May your hand be humiliated! You heard this from the Messenger of Allah but did not inform us of it?","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-946-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Munkar"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-946-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Daif"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-946-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Daif"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5d5","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":947,"bookHadithIndex":141,"text":"Jabir narrated:\"The Messenger of Allah performed Qaran for Hajj and Umrah, so he performed one Tawaf for both of them","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-947-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-947-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-947-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5d6","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":948,"bookHadithIndex":142,"text":"Ibn Umar narrated that:The Messenger of Allah said: \"Whoever assumes Ihram for Hajj and Umrah, then it is acceptable for him to perform one Tawaf and one Sa'I for them both, until he exits Ihram for both of them together","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-948-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-948-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-948-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5d7","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":949,"bookHadithIndex":143,"text":"Al-Ala bin Al-Hadrami narrated :(that the Prophet said): \"The Muhajir may stay for three (days) in Makkah after carrying out his rites","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-949-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-949-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-949-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-949-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5d8","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":950,"bookHadithIndex":144,"text":"Ibn Umar said:\"When the Prophet would come home from a battle, or Hajj, or Umrah, when he was it a tract of land or raised area he would say 'Allahu Akbar (Allah is Most Great)' three times, then say: 'La Ilaha illallah Wahdahu la sharika lahu, lahul-mulku wa lahul-Hamdu wa Huwa ala kulli shai'in qadir. A'ibuna ta'ibun abidun saa'ihuna li Rabbina Hamiduna, Sadaqallahu wa'dahu wa nasara abdahu wa hazamal-ahzab Wahdah. (None has the right to be worshiped but Allah Alone without partners. To Him belongs the sovereignty and to Him belongs the praise, and He has power over all things. We are returning, repenting, worshipping, traveling for our Lord, and we are praising. Allah has told the truth, and kept His promise and helped His worshipper, and routed the confederates, Alone)","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-950-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-950-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-950-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-950-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5d9","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":951,"bookHadithIndex":145,"text":"Ibn Abbas narrated:\"We were with the Messenger of Allah on a journey when he saw a man fall from his camel, his neck was broken and he died, and he was a Muhrim. So the Messenger of Allah said: 'Wash him with water and Sidr, and shroud him in his garments, and do not cover his head. For indeed he will be resurrected on the Day of Judgment saying the Talbiyah","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-951-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-951-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-951-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-951-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5da","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":952,"bookHadithIndex":146,"text":"Nubaih bin Wahb narrated that :Umar bin Ubaidullah bin Ma'mar was complaining about his eyes while he was a Muhrim. He asked Aban bin Uthman about it and he said: \"Bandage it with some aloes, for I heard Uthman bin Affan mentioning that the Messenger of Allah said: 'Bandage it with aloes","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-952-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-952-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-952-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-952-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Muslim"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5db","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":953,"bookHadithIndex":147,"text":"Abdur-Rahman bin Abu Laila narrated from Ka'b bin Ujrah that:The Prophet passed by him while he was at Al-Hudaibiyah, before entering Makkah, and he was a Muhrim. He had lit a fire under a cooking pot and lice were falling all over his face. So he (the Prophet) said: \"Have these lice of yours troubled you?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"Shave and feed six of the poor with a Faraq\" and a Faraq is three Sa - \"or fast three days, or slaughter a sacrifice.\" Ibn Abi Najih (one of the narrators) said: \"Or slaughter a sheep","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-953-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-953-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-953-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-953-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Bukhari And Muslim"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5dc","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":954,"bookHadithIndex":148,"text":"Abi Al-Baddah bin Adi narrated from his father:\"The Prophet permitted the shepherds to stone a day and leave a day","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-954-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-954-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-954-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5dd","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":955,"bookHadithIndex":149,"text":"Abi Al-Baddah bin Asim bin Adi narrated from his father:\"The Messenger of Allah permitted the camel herders who were in the camp (at Mina) to stone on the Day of An-Nahr then to gather the stoning of two days after the Day of An-Nahr, so that they stoned them during one of them.\" Malik said: \"I think that he said about the first of them: 'They they should stone on the day of departure","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-955-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-955-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-955-basharawadmaarouf","name":"Bashar Awad Maarouf","grade":"Hasan Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-955-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Sahih"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5de","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":956,"bookHadithIndex":150,"text":"Anas bin Malik narrated:\"When Ali returned to the Messenger of Allah from Yemen he said: 'For what did you intended the Talbiyah?' He replied: 'I intended the Talbiyah for what the Messenger of Allah announced it.' So he (pbuh) said: 'If I did not have the Hadi with me then I would exit Ihram","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-956-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-956-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-956-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih - Agreed Upon"}]},{"id":"69b6c745dd1a4c9c86f0b5df","editionId":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322","bookIndex":9,"hadithIndex":957,"bookHadithIndex":151,"text":"Ali narrated:\"I asked the Messenger of Allah about the day of Al-Hajj Al-Akbar and he said: 'They Day of An-Nahr","grades":[{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-957-ahmadmuhammadshakir","name":"Ahmad Muhammad Shakir","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-957-alalbani","name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"id":"69b55e8d6f42ba7ccb2a1322-9-957-zubairalizai","name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih"}]}]}